WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.330
At the start of 1960, the United
Nations had 82 member states.

2
00:00:05.380 --> 00:00:08.470
By the end of that year, it had 99.

3
00:00:08.520 --> 00:00:14.150
That's 17 new members in a single
year, and 16 of them in Africa.

4
00:00:14.200 --> 00:00:15.590
Did a war end?

5
00:00:15.640 --> 00:00:17.690
Did the UN change its rules?

6
00:00:17.740 --> 00:00:21.110
Why did so many African
countries join at once?

7
00:00:21.160 --> 00:00:25.610
In this mission, you'll explore what
gives a state supreme authority over its

8
00:00:25.660 --> 00:00:26.930
own territory.

9
00:00:26.980 --> 00:00:32.510
Then you'll see how, in 1947,
one territory became two states,

10
00:00:32.560 --> 00:00:36.150
India and Pakistan,
with a brand-new border.

11
00:00:36.200 --> 00:00:40.830
Your mission: explain why sixteen African
countries joined the United Nations

12
00:00:40.880 --> 00:00:42.370
in a single year.
